1
00:00:04,045 --> 00:00:05,255
(Howard:)How much time do we have?

2
00:00:05,422 --> 00:00:09,012
(Leonard:)Uh, T-minus five hours,
37 minutes to onset of meteor shower.

3
00:00:09,175 --> 00:00:13,595
(Raj:)Okay, our position
is 34.48 degrees north, 118.31 west.

4
00:00:13,763 --> 00:00:17,603
(Raj:)That means the azimuth
should be 168.22 degrees...

5
00:00:17,767 --> 00:00:21,647
(Raj:)...relative to magnetic north
with an elevation of 49.93.

6
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:23,483
(Howard:)-Anything yet?
-Uh, we have a signal...

7
00:00:23,648 --> 00:00:26,488
-...but no frame lock.
-Hang on. How about now?

8
00:00:26,651 --> 00:00:27,691
[JAZZ MUSIC PLAYING]

9
00:00:27,861 --> 00:00:31,701
We did it. Ha, ha.
We have the West Coast feed of HBO.

10
00:00:32,574 --> 00:00:35,244
(Howard:)Ooh, Real Sex.

11
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:37,160
(Raj:)Big deal. Every time I watch that...

12
00:00:37,328 --> 00:00:40,038
(Raj:)...it's old women putting condoms
on cucumbers.

13
00:00:40,457 --> 00:00:43,167
(Sheldon:)All right,
let's see what's on the East Coast feed.

14
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:45,921
(Leonard:)Oh, hey. Dune.

15
00:00:48,256 --> 00:00:52,506
(Raj:)Not a great movie,
but look at that beautiful desert.

16
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:56,010
(Leonard:)Too bad Sheldon couldn't come with us.

17
00:00:56,181 --> 00:00:58,061
It's just not the same without him.

18
00:00:58,516 --> 00:01:00,436
[ALL LAUGHING]

19
00:01:01,269 --> 00:01:03,149
LEONARD:
That was good. That was good.

20
00:01:03,313 --> 00:01:05,313
[HOWARD & LEONARD SIGH]

21
00:01:06,441 --> 00:01:08,941
(Howard:)Oh, this sucks.
I'm switching back to Real Sex.

22
00:01:12,155 --> 00:01:14,615
(Sheldon:)Sheldon's log.

23
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:18,285
(Sheldon:)Stardate 63345.3.

24
00:01:18,453 --> 00:01:22,043
(Sheldon:)While my colleagues are off
observing the Leonid meteor shower...

25
00:01:22,207 --> 00:01:24,457
...I've remained behind
to complete my paper...

26
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:27,796
(Sheldon:)...on the decays
of highly excited massive string states.

27
00:01:27,962 --> 00:01:29,882
(Sheldon:)Although my research is going well...

28
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:33,798
(Sheldon:)...I do miss the warmth
of human companionship.

29
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:39,019
[LAUGHS]

